{"id":"c96eb70b5fd08810","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-gaussian.md","title":"Gaussian Distribution","display":"df-gaussian — Gaussian Distribution","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-gaussian","aliases":["58-df-gaussian","Gaussian","Normal Distribution"],"display":"df-gaussian — Gaussian Distribution","depends_on":["[[../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md]]","[[../batch11/58-df-density-function.md]]","[[58-df-probability-space]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-gaussian"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-gaussian</span><span>Gaussian</span><span>Normal Distribution</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-gaussian — Gaussian Distribution"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"49ad0501f11b0cd1\" href=\"?note=49ad0501f11b0cd1\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md\">../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d4fc4686aaece886\" href=\"?note=d4fc4686aaece886\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-density-function.md\">../batch11/58-df-density-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"58-df-probability-space\">58-df-probability-space</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\((\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (probability space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R\">\\(X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R\\)</span> (random-variable candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m\\in\\mathbb R\">\\(m\\in\\mathbb R\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\">\\(v\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\)</span> (mean and positive variance parameters)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span> (Lebesgue measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S\\)</span> (random-variable predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DensityFunction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{DensityFunction}_S\\)</span> (density predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}\">\\(\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}\\)</span> (probability-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"58-df-probability-space\">58-df-probability-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\(\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (nondegenerate Gaussian predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gaussian} \\vdash \\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P) \\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S(X;(\\Omega,\\mathcal F),(\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)))\\land m\\in\\mathbb R\\land v\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\land\\exists\\mu\\;\\exists f\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}^{\\mathbb R}\\;\\Bigl(\\forall B\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\\;(\\mu(B)=\\mathbb P(X^{-1}[B]))\\land\\mathrm{DensityFunction}_S(f,\\mu,\\lambda,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\left(f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi v}}\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{(x-m)^2}{2v}\\right)\\right)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gaussian} \\vdash \\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P) \\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S(X;(\\Omega,\\mathcal F),(\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)))\\land m\\in\\mathbb R\\land v\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\land\\exists\\mu\\;\\exists f\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}^{\\mathbb R}\\;\\Bigl(\\forall B\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\\;(\\mu(B)=\\mathbb P(X^{-1}[B]))\\land\\mathrm{DensityFunction}_S(f,\\mu,\\lambda,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\left(f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi v}}\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{(x-m)^2}{2v}\\right)\\right)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Normal/Gaussian distribution</li>\n<li>Standard normal: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N(0, 1)\">\\(N(0, 1)\\)</span></li>\n<li>The identities <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb E[X]=m\">\\(\\mathbb E[X]=m\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Var}(X)=v\">\\(\\operatorname{Var}(X)=v\\)</span> are consequences of the density, not additional defining clauses.</li>\n<li>Central limit theorem: sums of i.i.d. converge to normal</li>\n<li>Stable under linear transformations</li>\n<li>Characteristic function: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\phi_X(t) = e^{i\\mu t - \\frac{\\sigma^2 t^2}{2}}\">\\(\\phi_X(t) = e^{i\\mu t - \\frac{\\sigma^2 t^2}{2}}\\)</span></li>\n<li>Brownian motion: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_t \\sim N(0, t)\">\\(B_t \\sim N(0, t)\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples</li>\n<li>Feller, An Introduction to Probability Theory</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md","status":"resolved","id":"49ad0501f11b0cd1","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-random-variable.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch11/58-df-density-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"d4fc4686aaece886","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-density-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-probability-space","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-probability-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-probability-space","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}$ (probability-space predicate, see [[58-df-probability-space]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"m\\in\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"v\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DensityFunction}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gaussian} \\vdash \\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P) \\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{ProbabilitySpace}(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\operatorname{RandomVariable}_S(X;(\\Omega,\\mathcal F),(\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)))\\land m\\in\\mathbb R\\land v\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\land\\exists\\mu\\;\\exists f\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}^{\\mathbb R}\\;\\Bigl(\\forall B\\in\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)\\;(\\mu(B)=\\mathbb P(X^{-1}[B]))\\land\\mathrm{DensityFunction}_S(f,\\mu,\\lambda,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R))\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\left(f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi v}}\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{(x-m)^2}{2v}\\right)\\right)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"N(0, 1)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb E[X]=m","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Var}(X)=v","display":false},{"tex":"\\phi_X(t) = e^{i\\mu t - \\frac{\\sigma^2 t^2}{2}}","display":false},{"tex":"B_t \\sim N(0, t)","display":false}],"bytes":2131,"backlinks":[{"id":"b01b13e1ea3167d2","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"a8a0a7253619eec2","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"8fc074624288fbbb","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Gaussian}_S(X;m,v;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ (nondegenerate Gaussian predicate, see [[58-df-gaussian]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-576","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-gaussian.md|58-df-gaussian]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["49ad0501f11b0cd1","d4fc4686aaece886","0578a357a86e9d8f"]}